<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luchuan–Pingmian campaigns</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1436">1436</a>–<a href="/years/1449">1449</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Luchuan–Pingmian campaigns were a series of Ming Chinese military expeditions from 1436 to 1449 against the Shan state of Mong Mao, called Luchuan by the Chinese, on the south-western frontier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a>. They were directed against the ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/si-renfa">Si Renfa</a>, who had expanded his power at the expense of other chiefdoms. After costly fighting he fled to Ava, which eventually handed him over, and Mong Mao was broken up.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luchuan-pingmian-campaigns.jpg" alt="Luchuan–Pingmian campaigns" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 瑞丽江的河水 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E9%BA%93%E5%B7%9D%E4%B9%8B%E5%BD%B9-%E6%80%BB%E5%9B%BE-%E8%8B%B1%E6%96%87%E7%89%88.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
